  "assessment": "The source provides a Landau-Peierls-type argument and perturbative RG analysis for the long-range XY model, yielding a renormalized BKT transition temperature T_BKT as a function of the long-range exponent sigma and coupling g. The key quantitative relation is T_BKT = (pi/4)(9 - 4 sigma + sqrt(49 + 16 pi g - 56 sigma + 16 sigma^2)), with sigma in the regime where long-range interactions are irrelevant (sigma > 2 - eta). The source also gives the critical temperature for long-range relevance T_c,lr = 2 pi (2 - sigma). The extraction focuses on the T_BKT relation as the primary quantitative cluster, with sigma as the control and T_BKT as the readout. The source does not report numerical values for sigma or T_BKT beyond the formula, so the control domain is symbolic (sigma > 2 - eta) and the readout is computed from the formula. The case is authoring-ready because the formula provides a deterministic response for any sigma in the stated regime.",
